From a3627938808a1a163f15a084b2304099ef4fd5f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:10:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 41/55] drm/gma500: free sgxfive GPU-reachable memory only
 after BIF flush

Pages of an unmapped range, page tables and page directories were freed
at once, while the BIF may still hold translations through them until a
kernel-CCB command carrying the invalidation has been processed. Put
them on a deferred list tagged with the next command's number, which
now carries INVAL_BIF_PT | _PD, and free each one when the EDM's read
offset has passed that command. A 10 ms reaper does the freeing and
sends PROCESS_QUEUES itself when no other command follows; with the
firmware halted the BIF is in reset and everything goes at once. The
range is reusable at once, since a stale translation still lands on
the pinned pages. KUnit covers the done count across the CCB wrap and
the in-order reaping.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive.c      | 79 ++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_priv.h | 23 ++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_vm.c   | 79 +++++++++++++++----
 .../gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_vm_test.c  | 54 ++++++++++++-
